cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Khepri — consumption-based hourly carbon intensity for the Nordic bidding zones, 2025"
message: "Cite this dataset and read the excluded-share caveats in README.md."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Nicolaysen"
    given-names: "Eirik Botten"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9188-6788"
    affiliation: "EcoDeco AS"
abstract: >-
  Hourly consumption-based (import-adjusted) carbon intensity for the nine Nordic
  bidding zones NO1-NO5 and SE1-SE4 for 2025, with FI, DK1 and DK2 as control zones.
  Derived by proportional-sharing flow tracing on ENTSO-E A11 physical cross-border
  flows across the whole ENTSO-E region (51 zones, 103 borders, 8760 hours), with
  emission factors applied to the traced mix afterwards. Two factor sets: Khepri v1's
  published IPCC AR5 lifecycle table and exclusion rules, and a proposed direct
  variant. Extends the production-based Khepri v1 dataset with the import-adjusted
  layer. Includes the tracing code, the v1 reproduction check, internal cross-checks,
  and an external validation against Google's published cloud-region figures.
keywords:
  - carbon intensity
  - consumption-based accounting
  - flow tracing
  - bidding zone
  - Norway
  - Sweden
  - ENTSO-E
  - carbon-aware computing
